\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  $\epsilon _{R}$ and $\epsilon _{A}$ transformations on the closed time path. $\epsilon _{R}$ translates the $a=1,2$ variables in the same direction while $\epsilon _{A}$ does in the opposite directions. Lagrangians without explicit $t$ dependence is invariant under $\epsilon _{R}$ translations only. As depicted in the right panel, equal-time 1-2 couplings are not equal-time anymore after the $\epsilon _A$-transformation.}}{13}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:TwoTimeTr}{{2}{13}{$\epsilon _{R}$ and $\epsilon _{A}$ transformations on the closed time path. $\epsilon _{R}$ translates the $a=1,2$ variables in the same direction while $\epsilon _{A}$ does in the opposite directions. Lagrangians without explicit $t$ dependence is invariant under $\epsilon _{R}$ translations only. As depicted in the right panel, equal-time 1-2 couplings are not equal-time anymore after the $\epsilon _A$-transformation}{figure.2}{}}
